.S. in 1924. In 1931, Bayer internationally removed it from its product palette. Subsequently, it internationally became an illegal drug and was produced only by the criminal sector - only in some countries like the United Kingdom, the chemical substance therein is still prescribed as a medicine for certain purposes, however not under the original brand name Heroin which belonged to Bayer.<br><br>\n<p>REMARK: It can be seen that the photographed item is a replica, hence no original from before about 1924/25 but produced later, as in the second line there is a spelling error (typo) in the word \"PHARMACUTICAL\" - a letter E is missing before the U.\n</p>\n<br>Outer dimensions of the photographed item including a wooden frame (which is not shown): 45\" x 34\" (114 cm x 86 cm).","source":"commons-desc-page"},"Artist":{"value":"Unknown author<span style=\"display: none;\">Unknown author</span>","source":"commons-desc-page"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/jpeg"}]},"103404729":{"pageid":103404729,"ns":6,"title":"File:Genuine Bayer Aspirin 1925.png","index":1,"imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"size":56642,"width":390,"height":553,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Genuine_Bayer_Aspirin_1925.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":640,"thumbheight":907,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Genuine_Bayer_Aspirin_1925.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":640,"height":907},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/36/Genuine_Bayer_Aspirin_1925.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Genuine_Bayer_Aspirin_1925.png","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.or